            "review_title": "Review at Kubara",
            "review_text": "siulin2018\nSingapore, Singapore46 contributions\n0\nWonderful Soups!\nAug 2018 • Friends\nThis is one my favourite restaurants. The food is flavourful and very fresh. The broths are the best! They are imported from Japan so everything is authentic, just like its restaurant in Kyushu. I usually have the mushroom hot pot with sesame miso broth at lunch but recently I was introduced to the onion chowder in flying fish broth. It was wonderful! Served with pork, chicken, lots of fresh greens. The other food on the menu like belly pork (butakakuni), chicken wings, grilled saba, salad with burdock, salmon sashimi and tempura, are good too. For the quality and freshness of ingredients, the prices are reasonable. I read about the bad service in other reviews but I have never encountered bad service at Kubara and I go there quite frequently. I will continue to go back!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten August 28, 2018",
            "rating": 5.0,
