            "review_text": "maryyeo\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam4531 contributions\n0\nFabulous Japanese soups\nNov 2016 • Friends\nLocated on the corner of the 5th floor, this restaurant has wide comfortable seating and lots of natural lights gushing in from a long stretch of full-glass windows. It's a pleasant place to go to meet friends or business partners for a quiet chat over some calming and wholesome good soups.\n\nAlthough set lunches are priced slightly above average i.e. at least usd15, it's still worth it because they're serving high quality, authentically prepared Japanese soups that are beautifully presented in the stone pots on their wooden trays. You can taste the freshness and sweetness in their soups from the good ingredients that they use and not from any artificial flavorings. Even the simple chawanmushi was filled with many ingredients and a delish broth, not the usual plain ones that you get elsewhere.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten October 31, 2017",
