            "review_title": "Review at Kubara",
            "review_text": "p911turbo\nTexas474 contributions\n0\nI loved it!\nJul 2017 • Family\nI had a lovely lunch with my very funny daughter who does not like food court style cuisines. After checking several restaurants, we decided to try this Japanese eatery because it looked quieter than other ones.\n\nCommunicating with them in English is still an issue but they were attentive and helpful.\n\nI had the chicken in broth. The chicken was a bit tough but I loved the broth which was not greasy and full of veggies. The udon noodles could be cooked a little longer to make them softer but overall I loved my choice!\n\nMy daughter had the Mango Calpis which was really yummy and the mushrooms in broth. Her broth was not greasy but creamy and she loved it. She said that everything tasted fresh. And she is a big veggie lover so the lunch made her so happy.\n\nIt was a beautiful lunch because it was quiet and we could talk and enjoy the ambience and food.\n\nAt the end of the lunch, the server gave us a coupon and asked us to come back! What a nice gesture! For your reference, the whole experience costed us about $US50.\nRead more\nWritten July 10, 2017",
